msgid "Transpile an LUCJ ansatz {#transpile-an-lucj-ansatz}"
msgstr "I-transpile ang isang LUCJ ansatz {#transpile-an-lucj-ansatz}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The concepts in this guide are only available in the Python API.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Ang mga konsepto sa gabay na ito ay available lamang sa Python API.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The local unitary cluster Jastrow ([LUCJ](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2023/sc/d3sc02516k)) ansatz is a compact, hardware-efficient parametrization of a correlated electronic wavefunction. It is a member of the more general unitary cluster Jastrow (UCJ) family and takes the form\n"
msgstr "Ang local unitary cluster Jastrow ([LUCJ](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2023/sc/d3sc02516k)) ansatz ay isang compact at hardware-efficient na parametrization ng isang correlated na electronic wavefunction. Miyembro ito ng mas pangkalahatang unitary cluster Jastrow (UCJ) na pamilya at may anyong\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\Psi \\rangle = \\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{L} \\mathcal{U}_k\\, e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}\\,\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger\\right) \\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\Psi \\rangle = \\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{L} \\mathcal{U}_k\\, e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}\\,\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger\\right) \\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle$ is a reference state (typically Hartree-Fock), each $\\mathcal{U}_k$ is an orbital rotation, and each $\\mathcal{J}_k$ is a diagonal Coulomb operator\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $\\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle$ ay isang reference state (karaniwang Hartree-Fock), ang bawat $\\mathcal{U}_k$ ay isang orbital rotation, at ang bawat $\\mathcal{J}_k$ ay isang diagonal Coulomb operator\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{J} = \\frac12 \\sum_{ij,\\sigma\\tau} \\mathbf{J}^{\\sigma\\tau}_{ij}\\,\n"
"n_{i\\sigma}\\, n_{j\\tau},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{J} = \\frac12 \\sum_{ij,\\sigma\\tau} \\mathbf{J}^{\\sigma\\tau}_{ij}\\,\n"
"n_{i\\sigma}\\, n_{j\\tau},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $n_{i\\sigma}$ the number operator on spatial orbital $i$ with spin $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr "na ang $n_{i\\sigma}$ ay ang number operator sa spatial orbital $i$ na may spin $\\sigma$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) builds the ansatz operator; this package turns it into a circuit and lowers that circuit onto qubits. This guide is about the second half of that sentence. The reason to make the trip is the lowering itself: ffsim’s own Qiskit gates are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation, whereas a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") carries no assumption about its fermion-to-qubit encoding, so the same ansatz can be synthesized through whichever encoding suits the target device.\n"
msgstr "Binubuo ng [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) ang ansatz operator; ginagawa ito ng package na ito na circuit at ibinababa ang circuit na iyon sa mga qubit. Ang gabay na ito ay tungkol sa ikalawang kalahati ng pangungusap na iyon. Ang dahilan para gawin ang biyaheng ito ay ang mismong pagbaba: ang sariling mga Qiskit gate ng ffsim ay partikular sa Jordan-Wigner transformation, samantalang ang isang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ay walang ipinapalagay tungkol sa fermion-to-qubit encoding nito, kaya ang parehong ansatz ay maaaring i-synthesize sa pamamagitan ng alinmang encoding na akma sa target na device.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ansatz operator therefore arrives here ready-made, and everything below is what happens to it afterwards: what the gate decomposes into, how it lowers through Jordan-Wigner, how it is matched to a device coupling map, and what a non-Jordan-Wigner lowering would still need. For building, parametrizing, or simulating a UCJ ansatz in the first place, see ffsim’s [own guides](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/how-to-guides/qiskit-lucj.html).\n"
msgstr "Kaya ang ansatz operator ay dumarating dito nang handa na, at lahat ng nasa ibaba ay ang nangyayari rito pagkatapos: kung saan nagde-decompose ang gate, paano ito bumababa sa pamamagitan ng Jordan-Wigner, paano ito itinutugma sa coupling map ng device, at ano pa ang kakailanganin ng isang non-Jordan-Wigner na pagbaba. Para sa pagbuo, pag-parametrize, o pag-simulate ng UCJ ansatz sa simula pa lang, tingnan ang [sariling mga gabay](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/how-to-guides/qiskit-lucj.html) ng ffsim.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [ffsim relationship guide](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation) for how the two packages divide the work, and the [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the pipeline stages used below.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang [gabay sa ugnayan sa ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation) kung paano naghahati ng trabaho ang dalawang package, at ang [gabay sa transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) para sa mga yugto ng pipeline na ginagamit sa ibaba.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Get an LUCJ operator from ffsim {#1-get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim}"
msgstr "1. Kumuha ng LUCJ operator mula sa ffsim {#1-get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ansatz is initialized from the amplitudes of a coupled-cluster singles and doubles (CCSD) calculation. Run restricted Hartree-Fock followed by CCSD for a hydrogen molecule in the `6-31g` basis, using [PySCF](https://pyscf.org/) for the quantum chemistry, then hand the amplitudes to ffsim’s [`from_t_amplitudes()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.from_t_amplitudes \"(in ffsim)\"). It performs a *double factorization* of the $t_2$ amplitudes to obtain the per-layer diagonal Coulomb matrices and orbital rotations, and derives an optional final orbital rotation from the $t_1$ amplitudes. The number of repetitions $L$ is whatever that factorization yields; `n_reps` truncates it, trading accuracy for a shallower circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang ansatz ay ini-initialize mula sa mga amplitude ng isang coupled-cluster singles and doubles (CCSD) na kalkulasyon. Magpatakbo ng restricted Hartree-Fock na sinundan ng CCSD para sa isang hydrogen molecule sa `6-31g` na basis, gamit ang [PySCF](https://pyscf.org/) para sa quantum chemistry, pagkatapos ay ibigay ang mga amplitude sa [`from_t_amplitudes()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.from_t_amplitudes \"(in ffsim)\") ng ffsim. Nagsasagawa ito ng *double factorization* ng mga $t_2$ amplitude para makuha ang mga diagonal Coulomb matrix at orbital rotation ng bawat layer, at kumukuha ng opsyonal na huling orbital rotation mula sa mga $t_1$ amplitude. Ang bilang ng mga pag-uulit na $L$ ay kung ano man ang ibigay ng factorization na iyon; ang `n_reps` ay nagpuputol nito, ipinagpapalit ang accuracy para sa mas mababaw na circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is where the ansatz stops being an ffsim concern. ffsim offers choices here that this package neither sees nor needs to know about, such as the variationally optimized (“compressed”) factorization behind `optimize=True`, or the parameter-vector packing that a variational optimizer drives. All of them produce the same kind of operator, and everything below works unchanged on any of them.\n"
msgstr "Dito humihinto ang ansatz bilang alalahanin ng ffsim. May mga pagpipilian ang ffsim dito na hindi nakikita o kailangang malaman ng package na ito, gaya ng variationally optimized (\"compressed\") na factorization sa likod ng `optimize=True`, o ang pag-pack ng parameter vector na minamaneho ng variational optimizer. Lahat ng ito ay gumagawa ng parehong uri ng operator, at gumagana nang walang pagbabago ang lahat ng nasa ibaba sa alinman sa mga ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Turn the operator into a fermionic circuit {#2-turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "2. Gawing fermionic circuit ang operator {#2-turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") gate wraps the operator and expresses it as a circuit over *fermionic modes*. The gate is a pure unitary carrying no reference of its own, so prepend an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate (built with [`from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\")) to supply the Hartree-Fock reference the ansatz is applied to.\n"
msgstr "Binabalot ng [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") gate ang operator at ine-express ito bilang circuit sa mga *fermionic mode*. Ang gate ay purong unitary na walang sariling reference, kaya magdagdag sa unahan ng [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate (binuo gamit ang [`from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\")) para ibigay ang Hartree-Fock reference na pinagpapatungan ng ansatz.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decomposing the circuit reveals its anatomy, and this is the representation the rest of the guide operates on. The [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate prepares the reference determinant, and each ansatz layer contributes an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") $\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger$, then $e^{i\\mathcal{J}_k}$ (an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") of the diagonal Coulomb operator $\\mathcal{J}_k$), then $\\mathcal{U}_k$, with a final [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") at the end. The orbital rotations act per spin sector, so each is placed on the alpha modes `0..norb` and the beta modes `norb..2*norb` independently.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng pag-decompose sa circuit ang anatomiya nito, at ito ang representasyong pinagtatrabahuhan ng natitirang bahagi ng gabay. Inihahanda ng [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate ang reference determinant, at ang bawat ansatz layer ay nag-aambag ng [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") $\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger$, pagkatapos ay $e^{i\\mathcal{J}_k}$ (isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ng diagonal Coulomb operator na $\\mathcal{J}_k$), pagkatapos ay $\\mathcal{U}_k$, na may huling [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") sa dulo. Ang mga orbital rotation ay kumikilos sa bawat spin sector, kaya ang bawat isa ay inilalagay sa mga alpha mode na `0..norb` at sa mga beta mode na `norb..2*norb` nang hiwalay.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The gates that the UCJ ansatz decomposes into.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The gates that the UCJ ansatz decomposes into.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every gate in that decomposition is still fermionic: [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") and [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") are defined on modes, and no qubit or Pauli operator has appeared yet. That is what leaves the encoding open, and it is the state the ansatz stays in until the synthesis stage picks one.\n"
msgstr "Fermionic pa rin ang bawat gate sa decomposition na iyon: ang [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") at [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ay naka-define sa mga mode, at wala pang lumilitaw na qubit o Pauli operator. Iyon ang nag-iiwang bukas sa encoding, at iyon ang estado na pananatilihan ng ansatz hanggang sa pumili ng isa ang synthesis stage.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each layer ends with $\\mathcal{U}_k$ and the next begins with $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$, so adjacent [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates could be merged into a single rotation. A transpilation pass performing this fusion is a planned future development.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang bawat layer ay nagtatapos sa $\\mathcal{U}_k$ at ang susunod ay nagsisimula sa $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$, kaya ang magkakatabing [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gate ay maaaring pagsamahin sa iisang rotation. Ang isang transpilation pass na gumagawa ng fusion na ito ay planong paunlarin sa hinaharap.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Choose a fermion-to-qubit encoding {#3-choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding}"
msgstr "3. Pumili ng fermion-to-qubit encoding {#3-choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit is still fermionic, and that is the point at which this package earns its place in the workflow. A [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") carries no assumption about how modes become qubits, so the encoding is a *synthesis-stage* choice rather than something baked into the ansatz. That is what this package adds over ffsim’s own Qiskit gates, which are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation.\n"
msgstr "Fermionic pa rin ang circuit, at iyon ang punto kung saan napapatunayan ng package na ito ang halaga nito sa workflow. Ang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ay walang ipinapalagay kung paano nagiging mga qubit ang mga mode, kaya ang encoding ay pagpiling nasa *synthesis stage* at hindi isang bagay na nakabaon sa ansatz. Iyon ang naidaragdag ng package na ito kumpara sa sariling mga Qiskit gate ng ffsim, na partikular sa Jordan-Wigner transformation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Jordan-Wigner alone you would not need this detour: ffsim ships [`UCJOpSpinBalancedJW`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW.html#ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW \"(in ffsim)\") and its siblings, which take a UCJ operator to a qubit circuit on their own. The reason to route the ansatz through a fermionic circuit is everything *else* an encoding can buy you. Local encodings, for instance, spend extra qubits to bound the Pauli weight of each term, which the [1D](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) and [2D](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) flow-set guides use to make a Trotter step’s two-qubit depth independent of the system size.\n"
msgstr "Para sa Jordan-Wigner lamang, hindi mo kailangan ang lakad na ito: may kasamang [`UCJOpSpinBalancedJW`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW.html#ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW \"(in ffsim)\") ang ffsim at ang mga kapatid nito, na kayang gawing qubit circuit ang UCJ operator nang mag-isa. Ang dahilan para idaan ang ansatz sa isang fermionic circuit ay ang lahat ng *iba pang* maibibigay ng isang encoding. Halimbawa, ang mga local encoding ay gumagastos ng karagdagang qubit para limitahan ang Pauli weight ng bawat term, na ginagamit ng mga flow-set na gabay sa [1D](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) at [2D](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) para gawing hindi nakadepende sa laki ng sistema ang two-qubit depth ng isang Trotter step.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a UCJ ansatz specifically, the synthesis stage has to cover two kinds of gate:\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang UCJ ansatz partikular, kailangang saklawin ng synthesis stage ang dalawang uri ng gate:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The diagonal Coulomb evolution.** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") is already encoding-agnostic: [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") takes a mapper function, so the $e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}$ layers lower through any encoding you can express as one. The [flow-set guides](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) show how to write one.\n"
msgstr "**Ang diagonal Coulomb evolution.** Ang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ay encoding-agnostic na: ang [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") ay tumatanggap ng mapper function, kaya ang mga layer na $e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}$ ay bumababa sa pamamagitan ng anumang encoding na maipapahayag mo bilang isa. Ipinapakita ng mga [flow-set na gabay](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) kung paano sumulat ng isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The orbital rotations and the Slater-determinant preparation.** Neither an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") nor the [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") that the leading [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and rotation fuse into (see below) is mapped to qubits as such. The [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass first breaks them down, in fermionic space, into [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates on one or two modes each (and, for the preparation, an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") of the reference), so any encoding that can map an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") handles them. Under Jordan-Wigner, the factors between adjacent modes become [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)objects at the qubit stage.\n"
msgstr "**Ang mga orbital rotation at ang paghahanda ng Slater determinant.** Ni ang [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") ni ang [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") na pinagsasamahan ng nangungunang [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") at rotation (tingnan sa ibaba) ay hindi ma-map sa mga qubit bilang ganoon. Unang binabasag ng [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass ang mga ito, sa fermionic space, tungo sa mga [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate sa isa o dalawang mode bawat isa (at, para sa preparation, isang [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") ng reference), kaya anumang encoding na kayang mag-map ng isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ay kayang humawak sa mga ito. Sa ilalim ng Jordan-Wigner, ang mga factor sa pagitan ng magkakatabing mode ay nagiging mga [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)object sa qubit stage.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The initialization.** The plugin for [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") is not parametrized by an encoding: it documents its assumption of an occupation-basis encoding with a 1-to-1 mode-to-qubit mapping, and emits gates directly on that basis. A different encoding needs its own plugin for it, and none ships yet.\n"
msgstr "**Ang initialization.** Ang plugin para sa [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") ay hindi pina-parametrize ng isang encoding: idinodokumento nito ang palagay nito na occupation-basis na encoding na may 1-to-1 na mode-to-qubit mapping, at direktang naglalabas ng mga gate sa basis na iyon. Ang ibang encoding ay nangangailangan ng sarili nitong plugin para dito, at wala pang kasama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to transpile UCJ circuits under a non-Jordan-Wigner encoding is an open research question and this package provides the framework within which to develop such a pipeline. The remainder of this guide constructs the transpiler pipeline for the Jordan-Wigner encoding, equivalent to the one produced by [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\"), as an example.\n"
msgstr "Ang paraan ng pag-transpile ng mga UCJ circuit sa ilalim ng non-Jordan-Wigner na encoding ay isang bukas na tanong sa pananaliksik at nagbibigay ang package na ito ng balangkas para mabuo ang ganoong pipeline. Ang natitirang bahagi ng gabay na ito ay bumubuo, bilang halimbawa, ng transpiler pipeline para sa Jordan-Wigner na encoding, katumbas ng ginagawa ng [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\").\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"lower-it-through-jordan-wigner\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Lower it through Jordan-Wigner {#4-lower-it-through-jordan-wigner}"
msgstr "4. Ibaba ito sa pamamagitan ng Jordan-Wigner {#4-lower-it-through-jordan-wigner}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lowering happens in [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"), which works like Qiskit’s [`HighLevelSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.HighLevelSynthesis): it walks the fermionic instructions and hands each to a plugin registered for that gate name. Its [`F2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.methods \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.methods\") attribute holds one [`F2QSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-f-2-q-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.F2QSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.F2QSynthesisPlugin\") per gate name, so building the stage means choosing a plugin for every fermionic gate the circuit contains:\n"
msgstr "Nangyayari ang pagbaba sa [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"), na gumagana tulad ng [`HighLevelSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.HighLevelSynthesis) ng Qiskit: dinadaanan nito ang mga fermionic instruction at ibinibigay ang bawat isa sa plugin na nakarehistro para sa pangalan ng gate na iyon. Ang [`F2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.methods \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.methods\") attribute nito ay may hawak na isang [`F2QSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-f-2-q-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.F2QSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.F2QSynthesisPlugin\") bawat pangalan ng gate, kaya ang pagbuo ng stage ay nangangahulugang pagpili ng plugin para sa bawat fermionic gate na nilalaman ng circuit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assigning instances like this is also how a plugin you wrote yourself enters the pipeline, without having to register it anywhere first.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-assign ng mga instance sa ganitong paraan ay siya ring paraan para makapasok sa pipeline ang plugin na isinulat mo mismo, nang hindi kailangang irehistro muna ito kahit saan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is where the encoding is settled, in the two ways section 3 described: explicitly, by handing [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") to [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), and implicitly, by the other plugin already assuming it.\n"
msgstr "Dito naisasaayos ang encoding, sa dalawang paraang inilarawan ng seksyon 3: tahasan, sa pamamagitan ng pagbibigay ng [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") sa [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), at hindi tahasan, sa pamamagitan ng isa pang plugin na ipinapalagay na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That stage then slots into a [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager) whose stages run in a fixed order:\n"
msgstr "Ang stage na iyon ay isinasalang sa isang [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager) na ang mga stage ay tumatakbo sa nakapirming pagkakasunod-sunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **optimization** stage runs *before* synthesis, on the fermionic circuit, which is what makes it worth having: it rewrites gates while they are still fermionic and encoding-agnostic, so the savings carry to whatever encoding follows. [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") collapses each run of consecutive [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates into one, which matters for a UCJ ansatz because every layer ends with $\\mathcal{U}_k$ and the next begins with $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$. [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") then fuses the leading [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and the rotation that follows it into a single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), which synthesis lowers through the cheaper reduced Slater decomposition instead of a full square rotation. The order matters: merging the rotations first exposes the single rotation immediately after the initialization, which the Slater fusion then contracts into it. [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") comes last, because it breaks up whatever rotation is left, and doing so any earlier would leave the two merging passes with nothing to fuse.\n"
msgstr "Ang **optimization** stage ay tumatakbo *bago* ang synthesis, sa fermionic circuit, na siyang dahilan kung bakit sulit ito: nire-rewrite nito ang mga gate habang fermionic at encoding-agnostic pa ang mga ito, kaya dala ng tipid ang anumang encoding na susunod. Pinagsasama ng [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") ang bawat sunod-sunod na [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gate sa isa, na mahalaga para sa UCJ ansatz dahil ang bawat layer ay nagtatapos sa $\\mathcal{U}_k$ at ang susunod ay nagsisimula sa $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$. Pagkatapos ay pinagsasama ng [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") ang nangungunang [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") at ang rotation na kasunod nito sa iisang [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), na ibinababa ng synthesis sa pamamagitan ng mas murang reduced Slater decomposition sa halip na buong square rotation. Mahalaga ang pagkakasunod-sunod: ang pagsasama muna ng mga rotation ay naglalantad ng iisang rotation kaagad pagkatapos ng initialization, na saka kinokontrata ng Slater fusion papasok dito. Ang [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") ang huli, dahil binabasag nito ang anumang rotation na natira, at kung gagawin ito nang mas maaga ay mawawalan ng pagsasamahin ang dalawang merging pass.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The remaining stages are plumbing. `input` and `output` convert between circuits and DAGs, `layout` assigns fermionic modes to qubits ([`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") maps mode `i` to qubit `i`), and `qubit` is an ordinary Qiskit pass manager that takes over once nothing fermionic is left.\n"
msgstr "Ang natitirang mga stage ay plumbing lamang. Ang `input` at `output` ay nagko-convert sa pagitan ng mga circuit at DAG, ang `layout` ay nag-a-assign ng mga fermionic mode sa mga qubit (ina-map ng [`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") ang mode `i` sa qubit `i`), at ang `qubit` ay isang ordinaryong Qiskit pass manager na pumapalit kapag wala nang natirang fermionic.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running it requires one preparatory step: the composite [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") gate has to be decomposed into its primitive gates first, so the optimization stage can see the individual rotations and evolutions.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpapatakbo nito ay nangangailangan ng isang hakbang sa paghahanda: ang composite na [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") gate ay kailangang i-decompose muna sa mga primitive na gate nito, para makita ng optimization stage ang mga indibidwal na rotation at evolution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without a target device, this maps onto `2 * norb` qubits with all-to-all connectivity assumed; the orbital rotations synthesize into [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)objects and the diagonal Coulomb evolutions into [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate)objects:\n"
msgstr "Kung walang target na device, nagma-map ito sa `2 * norb` na mga qubit na may ipinapalagay na all-to-all na connectivity; ang mga orbital rotation ay nasi-synthesize sa mga [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)object at ang mga diagonal Coulomb evolution sa mga [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate)object:\n"

